<string_table>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_barmen_1_has_documents_darkvalley_dialog_0">
        <text>About the documents from X-18, here they are.</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_barmen_1_has_documents_darkvalley_dialog_1">
        <text>Hand them over. Alright. The situation is clearing up. As I suspected, the Brain Scorcher is man-made. It's an experimental Kaymanov emitter; its parts were being manufactured right there in lab X-18. These documents contain a reference to lab X-16, where the finished units were sent. It's located on the territory of the factory complex near Lake Yantar. There's a scientist camp nearby, they can surely tell you more.</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_barmen_1_has_documents_darkvalley_dialog_2">
        <text>Go on.</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_barmen_1_has_documents_darkvalley_dialog_3">
        <text>It's not a simple situation: you need to get to the scientists and find out where lab X-16 is located to retrieve the missing part of the documents. Well, are you ready?</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_barmen_1_has_documents_darkvalley_dialog_4">
        <text>Of course.</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_barmen_1_has_documents_darkvalley_dialog_5">
        <text>Excellent. I'll be waiting.</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_barmen_1_has_documents_darkvalley_dialog_6">
        <text>...</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_barmen_go_to_darkvalley_dialog_0">
        <text>How are things with the documents? Learn anything?</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_barmen_go_to_darkvalley_dialog_1">
        <text>Here's the deal. Based on the documents you brought from Agroprom, things are starting to clear up, but we're missing data. There is a mention of a certain lab X-18, the description matches the abandoned underground facilities in the Dark Valley. You'll have to go there and retrieve the missing information. The lab is locked, and to open it, you'll need two electronic keys. I'll give you one, and you'll have to take the second one from Borov in the Dark Valley.</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_barmen_go_to_darkvalley_dialog_2">
        <text>Go on.</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_barmen_go_to_darkvalley_dialog_3">
        <text>All you need to do is get the second key to lab X-18, infiltrate it, and retrieve the missing part of the documents. Here, from me personally—suits with good radiation protection. You won't last long down there without them. Well, boys, will you take the job?</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_barmen_go_to_darkvalley_dialog_4">
        <text>Where else is there to go? It's foolish to turn back halfway.</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_barmen_go_to_military_dialog_0">
        <text>That's it, we have the prototypes. They work perfectly. Sakharov is a wizard.</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_barmen_go_to_military_dialog_1">
        <text>Well guys, all that's left is to deal with the "Scorcher" and the path to the North is open. Ready to move out?</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_barmen_go_to_military_dialog_2">
        <text>Ready!</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_barmen_go_to_military_dialog_3">
        <text>Listen up. You have the prototypes to protect you from the Scorcher. I know the coordinates of the bunker and I've sent them to your PDA. You must break through to the bunker under the antennas as quickly as possible and turn off the Scorcher. I don't know what happens next, but I feel it: it's worth it. I know one thing for sure: the road to the center of the Zone will be open. Good luck!</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_barmen_go_to_military_dialog_4">
        <text>See you.</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_trader_barmen_where_else_can_I_earn_money_dialog_0">
        <text>Who else can offer work?</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_trader_barmen_where_else_can_I_earn_money_dialog_1">
        <text>There are a couple of guys here: the hunter Pavlik, the mechanic-electrician Senka, Arny.</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_trader_barmen_where_else_can_I_earn_money_dialog_2">
        <text>Can you tell me more about Pavlik?</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_trader_barmen_where_else_can_I_earn_money_dialog_3">
        <text>Can you tell me more about Senka?</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_trader_barmen_where_else_can_I_earn_money_dialog_4">
        <text>Pavlik is our local retired hunter. He used to track and kill particularly dangerous mutants. Now he sits at his place among taxidermy trophies and hands out tasks; they say he pays pretty well. You can ask him.</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_trader_barmen_where_else_can_I_earn_money_dialog_5">
        <text>He sits in our garage and builds things. Buys up all sorts of junk from stalkers. A scavenger, in a word.</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_trader_barmen_where_else_can_I_earn_money_dialog_6">
        <text>Got it, thanks.</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_trader_barmen_where_else_can_I_earn_money_dialog_7">
        <text>Can you tell me more about Arny?</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_trader_barmen_where_else_can_I_earn_money_dialog_8">
        <text>He organizes fights at the arena and takes bets. You can participate too.</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_informant_break_dialog_0">
        <text>I'll think about it.</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_informant_start_dialog_0">
        <text>So, stalker. What brought you to me? Want to buy information? Or maybe sell some?</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_vlad_volchara_break_dialog_0">
        <text>See you.</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_vlad_volchara_good_story_dialog_0">
        <text>Hey, stalker, what the hell do you need a cake for?</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_vlad_volchara_good_story_dialog_1">
        <text>What business is it of yours? Who are you anyway?</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_vlad_volchara_good_story_dialog_2">
        <text>Don't get heated, I'm not asking out of malice. I'm genuinely interested.</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_vlad_volchara_good_story_dialog_3">
        <text>It's my birthday, a friend dragged this cake in. Ordered it from the Barman.</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_vlad_volchara_good_story_dialog_4">
        <text>Good friend. Did you come to the Zone together, or did you become buddies here? Care to tell the story?</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_vlad_volchara_good_story_dialog_5">
        <text>Eh, alright. My name is Vlad, but everyone calls me Volchara. Once, I lived in a city called Kislovodsk. Studies, work—everything went as usual. At 28, I married the charming Olesya; the wedding was top-notch, the whole works. And then—the terrible explosion at the CNPP. Since then, my hometown started being called the Doomed City.</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_vlad_volchara_good_story_dialog_6">
        <text>Doomed City? I've heard something like that.</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_vlad_volchara_good_story_dialog_7">
        <text>Uh-huh. When it blew, I was completely lost, didn't know what to do or where to go. But luckily, I had a loyal friend named Danya Voron. The guy has a good head on his shoulders! He's always ready to help and offer a way out of any mess. So we decided to get out of the Doomed City. Our journey was long and hard, but we finally made it to the Zone.</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_vlad_volchara_good_story_dialog_8">
        <text>Quite a story, you guys had it rough. Where are you headed next?</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_vlad_volchara_good_story_dialog_9">
        <text>I'm waiting for my friend, Danya Voron, to return from a raid. He said he knows where to get some good body armor! When he gets back, we'll celebrate my birthday, have a bite, prep our gear, and hit the road in search of new adventures. And you know, good friends are more valuable than all the artifacts in the Zone.</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_vlad_volchara_good_story_dialog_10">
        <text>Good luck in the Zone, bye!</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_stalker_vlad_volchara_start_dialog_0">
        <text>What do you need?</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_trader_barmen_has_documents_agroprom_dialog_0">
        <text>Stay healthy. We have the documents. And here's something else—Strelok's flash drive. Heard of him?</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_trader_barmen_has_documents_agroprom_dialog_1">
        <text>Strelok? I've heard. Not a stalker—a legend! Great work, guys. Now I need to sort through this mess, maybe I'll figure out how to break through to the North. Hand over the case.</text>
    </string>
    <string id="bar_smart_terrain_1_trader_barmen_has_documents_agroprom_dialog_2">
        <text>Take it.</text>
    </string>
